    "evidence_text": "Increased sensitivity of antigen-experienced T cells through the enrichment of oligomeric T cell receptor complexes.\n\nCa2+ messages are broadly important in cellular signal transduction.\n\nIn immune cells, Ca2+ signaling is an essential step in many forms of activation.\n\nThese signals were blocked by the intracellular Ca2+ buffer BAPTA.\n\nOur findings suggest that Ca2+ microdomains are due to an active signaling process.\n\nThe activation of T cells is the fundamental on switch for the adaptive immune system.\n\nDifferentiation of effector CD4 T cell populations (*).\n\nGolli protein negatively regulates store depletion-induced calcium influx in T cells.\n\nCalcium influx is crucial for T cell activation and differentiation.\n\nThe detailed regulation of this process remains unclear.\n\nGolli-deficient T cells were hyperproliferative and showed enhanced calcium entry upon T cell receptor stimulation.\n\nWe further found that golli regulates calcium influx in T cells through the inhibition of the store depletion-induced calcium influx.\n\nWe identified a critical differentiation period that required interactions between primed T cells.\n\nMemory CD4+ T cells induce innate responses independently of pathogen\n\nExpression of Golli mRNA during development in primary immune lymphoid organs of the rat",
